   1:App/Src/dut_app.c **** /**
   2:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  * [v0.2]
   3:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  * @file    dut_app.c
   4:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  * @brief   NUCLEO-H533RE loopback DUT: I2C1 master drives test patterns that
   5:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *          the PC sends; I2C2 (R1) and I2C3 (R2) answer as responders with the
   6:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *          synthetic register map. All three sit on ONE external bus, which
   7:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *          the sniffers under test also watch.
   8:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *
   9:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *          Isolated instrument: shares no code with the sniffer tools.
  10:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *          Protocol: loopback_dut/docs/PROTOCOL.md. Register map: dut_regmap.h.
  11:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *
  12:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  * Concurrency model
  13:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *   - Main loop: UART line assembly, command execution, master transfers
  14:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *     (interrupt-driven HAL Seq API, waited on with a TIM2 timeout).
  15:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *   - I2C2/I2C3 ISRs: responder byte streams (HAL listen + Seq, one byte at a
  16:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *     time so the stream can be computed on the fly and clock stretching can
  17:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *     be injected before any byte).
  18:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *   - Clock-stretch injection busy-waits inside the responder ISR: the HAL
  19:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *     clears ADDR / loads TXDR only after the callback returns, so SCL is held
  20:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *     low for the wait. Stretch therefore happens at byte boundaries only; a
  21:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  *     hardware I2C slave cannot stretch mid-byte.
  22:App/Src/dut_app.c ****  */
  23:App/Src/dut_app.c **** #include <stdio.h>
  24:App/Src/dut_app.c **** #include <string.h>
  25:App/Src/dut_app.c **** 
  26:App/Src/dut_app.c **** #include "main.h"
